    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0332" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1088.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-10T13:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is no question in my judgment but that the $500,000 will enable Dominican
                    Government to live and enact the reforms suggested by you. Hasten appointment of
                    commercial attaché.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
